      "title": "FAIRsharing: Data and Metadata Standards and Data Policies for Biomedical Research",
      "abstract": "This FAIRsharing System Biology Collection represents the (meta)data standards, repositories, databases and knowledgebases described in this article. FAIRsharing guides both consumers and producers of data to discover, select and use these resources with confidence, and resource maintainers to make their resource more discoverable, widely adopted and cited. This FAIRsharing Collection provided an at-a-glance view of these resources and their relationships, highlighting the activities of the system medicine community around reporting guidelines, terminologies, models and formats and their subsequent implementation in management and stewardship systems.",
